<title>USA: Central Vermont restructuring to cost 97 jobs.</title>
<headline>Central Vermont restructuring to cost 97 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>RUTLAND, Vt. 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Vermont Public Service Corp said Tuesday that it plans to restructure the company into five new business units, which will result in a staff reduction of 97 employees over the next 18 months.</p>
<p>Central Vermont said that it will be composed of a distribution company, a generation company, a retail sales company, an unregulated generation development company and a service company, which will support the other four units.</p>
<p>The company said it is also offering early retirement and voluntary redundancies to the affected workers on terms it said were significantly better than those made in 1994, when it cut its staff by about 20 percent.</p>
</text>
